{% comment %}
  Five stars, drawn twice and stacked: an empty row underneath and a mustard row
  on top, clipped to --cfl-stars-fill (set on the parent .cfl-stars). That one
  percentage covers both a whole-star review and a 4.9 overall score without
  any partial-star artwork.

  Decorative only. The parent hides it from screen readers and puts the rating
  in words next to it.

  Usage:
    <span class="cfl-stars" style="--cfl-stars-fill: 80%;" aria-hidden="true">
      {% render 'cfl-google-review-stars', star_id: section.id %}
    </span>

  star_id is the section ID; the star shape is a <symbol> the section draws
  once with the id "cfl-star-{star_id}".
{% endcomment %}

{%- capture row -%}
  {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" focusable="false"><use href="#cfl-star-{{ star_id }}"/></svg>
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<span class="cfl-stars__row cfl-stars__row--empty">{{ row }}</span>
<span class="cfl-stars__row cfl-stars__row--full">{{ row }}</span>
